zen_at":1792769909,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-23T15:38:29Z","frozen_sha":"ea89dabf2fb76aaa85afeb013a7be2a11815ea1e","head_ref":"copilot/http-getter-implementation","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":39979974840},"loop_kind":"pr_conflict_resolver","merge_base_sha":"4aa36d6e45604cb01e41b62615e3684ecddc44b6","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nHTTP client and server extractors now use `getErrorType()` as the final `error.type` value: an override's `null` omits the attribute, even for an HTTP error status. Getter defaults preserve role-specific status classification, exception-class fallback, and `_OTHER` for missing or non-positive status.\n\n- **Defaults:** Client errors begin at 400; server errors begin at 500. Successful responses without exceptions omit `error.type`.\n- **Overrides:** Return `null` to omit intentionally, or delegate to the inherited default to retain its classification:\n\n```java\n@Override\npublic String getErrorType(Request request, Response response, Throwable error) {\n  if (shouldOmitErrorType(request, response, error)) {\n    return null;\n  }\n  return HttpClientAttributesGetter.super.getErrorType(request, response, error);\n}\n```\n\n- **Compatibility:** Reactor Netty and Spring WebFlux retain their cancellation classification and delegate other cases to the defaults.","title":"Make HTTP getters own final error.type classification"},"mode":"publish","pr":20881,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792769911,"generation":2,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"490a2fa428cc484f95c1802fae08d445","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumen